<section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-8">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
    <div>
      <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-label text-muted">Self-describing deploy · <%= @app.name %></div>
      <h1 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink">Deploy config (Kamal · ADR 0001)</h1>
    </div>
    <%= link_to "Back", @app, class: "inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-border bg-surface px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-body hover:bg-fill" %>
  </div>

  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">
    Real, literal deploy coordinates generated from this app — no placeholder <code class="font-mono">ENV[…] || default</code> fallbacks.
    Commit these to the repo so <code class="font-mono">kamal console -d production</code> and
    <code class="font-mono">kamal app logs -d production</code> work by hand, with Conductor offline.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-4 rounded-large border border-border bg-bg-alt p-4">
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <div>
        <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">Self-describing deploy · <%= @app.self_describing? ? "enabled" : "off" %></div>
        <div class="mt-0.5 text-xs text-muted">
          <% if @app.self_describing? %>
            Deploys write these files into the checkout and run <code class="font-mono">kamal deploy -d production</code>.
          <% else %>
            Off — this app deploys the current way. Enabling makes Conductor write these files and deploy with <code class="font-mono">-d production</code>. Verify <code class="font-mono">kamal console -d production</code> works from the repo first.
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
      <%= button_to(@app.self_describing? ? "Disable" : "Enable", toggle_self_describing_app_path(@app), method: :patch,
            class: "shrink-0 rounded-lg border border-border bg-surface px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-body hover:bg-fill",
            form: { data: { turbo_confirm: (@app.self_describing? ? nil : "Enable self-describing deploy? The next deploy will use -d production.") } }) %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <% @files.each do |path, content| %>
    <div class="mt-6 rounded-large border border-border bg-surface shadow-soft">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-border px-4 py-2">
        <span class="font-mono text-sm text-ink"><%= path %></span>
        <% if path.include?("secrets") %>
          <span class="text-2xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-label text-warning">git-safe pointers · no raw values</span>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <pre class="overflow-x-auto p-4 text-xs text-body font-mono whitespace-pre-wrap"><%= content %></pre>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <div class="mt-6 rounded-large border border-border bg-bg-alt p-4 text-xs text-muted">
    <div class="font-semibold text-ink">To use</div>
    <ol class="mt-2 list-decimal space-y-1 pl-4">
      <li>Commit both files to the app repo — <code class="font-mono">.kamal/secrets.production</code> holds <em>pointers</em>, not secrets, so it's safe to commit.</li>
      <li>Seed the vault once: <code class="font-mono">localvault set <%= @app.slug %>.&lt;KEY&gt; &lt;value&gt; --vault devops</code> (or point the secrets file at a seeded <code class="font-mono">.env</code> to avoid per-command vault unlocks).</li>
      <li>Deploy / operate with the destination: <code class="font-mono">kamal deploy -d production</code>, <code class="font-mono">kamal console -d production</code>.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
